<div class="section-body">
  <div class="section-body-inner">
    <p>Access to education is now seen as a fundamental right. In many cases, it's the government's duty to provide it.</p>
    <p>But formal education is a very recent phenomenon. In the chart, we see the share of the adult population — those older than 15 — who has received some basic education and those who haven't.</p>
    <p>In the early 1800s, fewer than 1 in 5 adults had some basic education. Education was a luxury; in all places, it was only available to a small elite.</p>
    <p>But you can see that this share has grown dramatically, such that this ratio is now reversed. Less than 1 in 5 adults has not received any formal education.</p>
